        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.138,
            0.803,
            0.158
          ],
          "content": "Now, $\\mathrm { P Q } \\parallel \\mathrm { E F }   \\mathrm { a n d }   \\Delta   \\mathrm { A B C } \\cong \\Delta   \\mathrm { D P Q }$ (How ?)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.163,
            0.66,
            0.183
          ],
          "content": "So, $\\angle \\mathrm{A} = \\angle \\mathrm{D}, \\angle \\mathrm{B} = \\angle \\mathrm{P}   and   \\angle \\mathrm{C} = \\angle \\mathrm{Q}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.188,
            0.796,
            0.209
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, $\\Delta   \\mathrm { A B C } \\sim \\Delta   \\mathrm { D E F }$ (Why?)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.214,
            0.782,
            0.234
          ],
          "content": "We now take some examples to illustrate the use of these criteria."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.246,
            0.745,
            0.267
          ],
          "content": "Example 4 : In Fig. 6.29, if PQ ∥ RS, prove that ∆ POQ ∼ ∆ SOR."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.352,
            0.279,
            0.642,
            0.427
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.448,
                0.434,
                0.55,
                0.453
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 6.29"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_18_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.464,
            0.467,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": "Solution : $\\mathrm { P Q } \\parallel \\mathrm { R S }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.489,
            0.474,
            0.51
          ],
          "content": "So, $\\angle \\mathrm{P} = \\angle \\mathrm{S}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.718,
            0.49,
            0.898,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": "(Alternate angles)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.514,
            0.478,
            0.535
          ],
          "content": "and $\\angle Q = \\angle R$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.539,
            0.9,
            0.561
          ],
          "content": "Also, $\\angle POQ = \\angle SOR$ (Vertically opposite angles)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.564,
            0.504,
            0.585
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, $\\Delta  POQ  \\sim \\Delta  SOR$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.647,
            0.565,
            0.899,
            0.586
          ],
          "content": "(AAA similarity criterion)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.597,
            0.585,
            0.618
          ],
          "content": "Example 5 : Observe Fig. 6.30 and then find $\\angle \\mathrm { P } .$"
